  "solution": "**Given:**\n\n11 (1/2) + 12 (1/2) + 13 (1/2) + 14 (1/2)\n\n**Formula used:**\n\nAddition of mixed fractions:\n\nFor any mixed fraction a (b/c), convert it to improper fraction as (ac + b)/c\n\n**Calculation:**\n\n11 (1/2) = (11×2 + 1)/2 = 23/2\n\n12 (1/2) = (12×2 + 1)/2 = 25/2\n\n13 (1/2) = (13×2 + 1)/2 = 27/2\n\n14 (1/2) = (14×2 + 1)/2 = 29/2\n\n⇒ 23/2 + 25/2 + 27/2 + 29/2\n\n⇒ (23 + 25 + 27 + 29)/2\n\n⇒ 104/2\n\n⇒ 52\n\n**∴ The correct answer is option (1).**",
